Z||000000||Harry||01-28-2000||10:33 PM||||Well after much cursing, hand bashing etc.etc. I finally got the tranny away from the motor (yes the whole cradle is on the ground now) After all the crude you have to disconnect just to pull the motor away I think next time I would just pull the tranny alone. Seem's like it would have been less time consuming. My fuel lines would not break at the hoses so had to pull the plenum apart to discon from the rail. Then starter to pull inspection cover. Then broke the bolts on the manifolds to pull the connecter pipe.<BR>At any rate after taking the bolts off the pressure plate all, I do mean all the clutch plate spring fell to the ground!!!!<BR>The T. out bearing has a very deep groove and the fingers of the p.plate are basicaly worn flat as compared to the new plate there rounded. Got the assembly back together and tomorrow will have the cradle back into the compartment again. Hopefuly will be driving again by Sunday. Thanks for all the info everyone you have all been helpful as I knew you would.||||reg||14
